# Shell scripts are executed inside the Linux build containers, which mount this
# working tree directly rather than checking it out themselves. With
# core.autocrlf=true a Windows working copy would hand those scripts CRLF
# endings, and bash stops on the second line of every one of them:
#   set: pipefail\r: invalid option name
# Pinning them to LF keeps the mounted scripts runnable from any host.
*.sh text eol=lf
scripts/appimage/AppRun text eol=lf
